# JavaScript

Vanilla ES modules — no bundler, no framework. Match existing files.

## Module boundaries

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `config.js` | Default watchlist seed + tunable constants |
| `watchlist.js` | localStorage load/save/add/remove for watchlist |
| `api.js` | data.gov.hk fetch, format, session cache |
| `cache.js` | localStorage read/write with TTL |
| `estimate.js` | Bus position math, polyline helpers |
| `routing.js` | OSRM road snapping + cache |
| `map.js` | Full-bleed Leaflet map, idle GPS follow, focus overlays, active-area fit |
| `picker.js` | Add-flow map for stop selection |
| `geo.js` | Geolocation watch + listeners |
| `theme.js` | Light/dark + HK solar schedule |
| `app.js` | DOM orchestration only — no API URLs here |

## Naming

- `camelCase` functions and variables
- `UPPER_SNAKE` for exported config constants
- Watchlist entries: `id`, `route`, `stopId`, `direction`, `label`

## Patterns

- `async/await` for I/O; use `readCache`/`writeCache` for localStorage
- In-memory `Map` for session caches (`api.js`, `routing.js`)
- Tunables go in `config.js`, not scattered in feature modules
- DOM: build elements in JS (`createRowElement`), `data-id` on rows, delegate on `#cards`
- Focus/map async: cancel stale work with `focusToken` + `selectionKey()` pattern
- Map stage: `initMapStage` mounts Leaflet on boot; idle mode uses `followYouInActiveArea` (Maps/Uber-style: always move you marker; recenter into top half via single animated `setView` with projected south offset only when you leave the soft `IDLE_FOLLOW_WINDOW` around the top-half center, or on first fix / `force`); focus mode uses `activeAreaPadding` (~50% bottom inset, extra top for stop labels) in `fitBounds` / `scheduleFitToMarkers` so you + stop(s) + bus(es) frame above the watch-sheet; boarding pins use `stopIcon({ selected, label: nameEn, colorIndex })` for a glass name tooltip (deduped by stop id across multi-focus); any number of routes may be focused (colors cycle 6-entry `ROUTE_COLORS`); you marker stays visible whenever GPS is available; `setFocusedRows` syncs `#add-route-btn` to `nav-dock__add--clear` (click → `exitFocus`); `hideFocusPanel` clears route overlays and resumes idle follow (map never unmounts); `isFocusPanelVisible` means route focus is active, not that the map exists
- Focus estimate merge: `loadEstimateForEntry` preserves `boardingStop.nameEn` when the estimate object omits it
- Focus map viewport: `scheduleFitToMarkers` (double rAF after `invalidateSize`) frames stop + bus + you on select; also when the bus or you marker first appears
- Bus tracking: `api.trackingNowMs()` advances Citybus snapshot time; `estimate.resolveActiveBoardingEta` hands off to `second` when `first` is past; `estimate.matchBusEta` picks the earliest upstream ETA before boarding that is travel-time plausible vs boarding (`dist / Δt ≤ MAX_BUS_SPEED_M_PER_MIN`) — not latest-before-boarding — so following buses on multi-bus routes cannot anchor the chain; `estimate.buildEtaChain` sanitizes via exported `sanitizeEtaChain` (monotonic time-vs-distance) and drops implausible upstream points; `passedStopFloor` floors placement after passed upstream stops (same plausible matcher); `app.trackingFloor` = max(passed-stop floor, `progressHighWaterCum − MAX_BUS_REWIND_M`) so same-bus ETA slips may rewind at most `MAX_BUS_REWIND_M` and cannot walk back to the terminus; `bumpProgressHighWater` raises furthest progress shown (reset on `busChanged`); when a revised API prediction differs from the current marker by ≥ `BUS_REPOSITION_MIN_M`, `startBusReposition` lerps `cumDist` along the polyline for `BUS_REPOSITION_MS` (ease-out) then resumes tracking — forward or capped back, no freeze/teleport for same-bus; `estimate.positionFromEtaChain()` for segment placement (before-first also uses boarding ETA × speed from a plausible first→next segment or `DEFAULT_BUS_SPEED_M_PER_MIN` so terminus noise cannot pin at cumDist 0); lightweight focus ETA updates must not rewind `trackingNowMs` (keep `receivedAtMs` when `snapshotMs` unchanged); same-bus boarding ETA revisions update in place and may start reposition; re-run `sanitizeEtaChain` or trigger full refresh on real handoff; when boarding ETA ≤ `ARRIVING_THRESHOLD_MIN`, lightweight updates and the rAF loop snap the marker to the boarding stop (`reason: "arriving"`); focus mode passes `denseUpstream: true`
- Focus refresh tiers: 5 s row poll → `applyLightweightFocusEtaUpdate()` (boarding clock only without rewinding `receivedAtMs`, arriving snap under threshold, reposition to new prediction, or full refresh on handoff); full `refreshFocusedEstimate({ refreshUpstream: true })` on `snapshotMs` change, `FOCUS_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS`, animation ETA expiry, or active-bus handoff — preserves `receivedAtMs` when `snapshotMs` unchanged; same-bus keeps marker, preserves `progressHighWaterCum`, and repositions along route with rewind capped by `trackingFloor`; on `busChanged` / cleared marker: `clearBusReposition` + `stopBusAnimation` then `dissolveBusMarker` (marker freezes — `setBusMarkerPosition` ignores latlng while `focus-marker--dissolving`); `busAppearing` soft-spawns the next bus; do not preserve `prior.busLatLng` across `no-eta` or bus identity change
- Upstream ETAs: `fetchEta(..., { useCache: true, cacheTtlMs: UPSTREAM_ETA_CACHE_TTL_MS })` unless `refreshUpstream`
- Add-flow sheet: paint-first open — unhide sheet, `await` one `requestAnimationFrame`, then focus; idle-prefetch `fetchRoutes` (in-memory only); typeahead filters catalog and renders at most 8 suggestions — never a full-route datalist DOM; `showAddMapPreview()` mounts a dimmed non-interactive map (`add-sheet__map--dimmed`) centered on you/`LOCATION` until a direction is chosen; preview passes `isStale` tied to `loadToken` so a direction click cannot be wiped by a late preview paint
- Add-flow sheet: cancel stale map loads with `loadToken` (same idea as `focusToken`); on direction select remove `--dimmed` and paint stops immediately, then `roadSnapStopsChunked` + `setPickerPath` to upgrade the line; clearing route restores dimmed preview while the sheet stays open; `fitPickerBounds` / `scheduleFitPicker` frames you-only or the path after layout; `showPickerMap({ isStale })` bails before `clearPickerLayers` when superseded
- Swallow errors only at prefetch/UI boundaries; `console.warn` for focus/estimate failures

## Adding code

Extend the owning module. Do not add dependencies or a build step.

## When shipping JS changes

Update this file if you add a module, shift responsibilities, or introduce a new pattern. Also update `docs/PRD.md` per [workflow.mdc](workflow.mdc) — same turn, no prompt needed.
